.org/blog/focus-your-mind-on-motherhood  \n\nFor more information: Lori K. Mihalich-Levin, JD, founder of Mindful Return and creator of the Mindful Return E-Course and blog, is Mama to two beautiful red-headed boys (ages 1 1/2 and 4) and is the Director of Hospital and GME Payment Policies at the Association of American Medical Colleges (AAMC).  She founded Mindful Return to give new Mamas the tools they need to plan a peaceful, thoughtful, and successful return to work after maternity leave.  Lori has been committed to promoting women’s equality and leadership throughout her career. Lori loves tickling her cuddly boys, reading them Cars Galore Cars thousands of times, sharing parenting adventures with her amazing husband, building supportive communities, and practicing yoga at lil omm.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAbout Mindful Return - Mindful Return (https://www.mindfulreturn.com/about/)\nciteturn84search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 12.5 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; \n\n# Mindful Return is a global movement that helps new moms and dads navigate the uncertain terrain of working parenthood.\n\n## Are you ready to trade your working parent guilt for meaningful connection and support?\n\nImage\n\n## Imagine feeling confident about your decisions both as a\n parent and a professional.\n\n## And having a whole set of tools to use when the inevitable\noverwhelm, guilt, uncertainty, and fatigue sets in.\n\n# Mindful Return makes this vision a reality.\n\niframe\n\n## The Ultimate Guide to Prep You for Parental Leave\n\nOur FREE guide, 99 Questions to Ask Yourself Before, During, and After Parental Leave, is our gift to you and your new bundle of joy. At Mindful Return, we know that calm, thoughtful planning, and time for reflection, are keys to success in working parent life.\n\n#### As featured in the Washington Post: “Transitioning back to work after a new baby? Now there’s a class just for that.”\nA bit terrified, at times.  Committed to growth.  Loyal to our fellow working parents.  And compassionate.\n\nWhat is Mindful Return committed to?  \n\n  * Helping new parents feel calm, supported, confident, and connected.\n  * Challenging the workplace status quo.\n  * Helping employers retain their new parent talent.\n  * Diversity and respect for differences.\n  * Inclusion of all voices, with a warm welcome to BIPOC, LGBTQ, single, adoptive, and single-mom-by-choice parents.\n  * Lifelong connections to other working parents.\n\nHow does Mindful Return live this mission?\n\n  * Through two 4-week online programs that focus on the following themes: (1) a mindful mindset for returning to work after baby; (2) managing all the logistics; (3) growing leadership skills as a new parent; and (4) building communities of other working parents.  More about the mom version of this program is here.  More about the dad version is here.  More about the version of the program for parents of children with special needs is here.\n  * By helping 80+ employers provide the Mindful Return courses to their employees as an innovative benefit and by holding workshops with groups of employees.\n  * By connecting all Mindful Return course alumnae to one another through private Facebook and LinkedIn community and monthly calls.\n  * Through Lori’s book, Back to Work After Baby: How to Plan and Navigate a Mindful Return from Maternity Leave.\n  * By providing timely and topical advice through a weekly blog post and weekly newsletter called “Saturday Secrets”.\n\nBecoming a working parent shouldn’t be something you have to “get through” but something you get to create. You’ll return to work a different person you than when you left, with new skills that are – yes indeed – useful at the office. You’ll have different priorities. Different goals. And likely you’ll be sleep deprived those first few months and just trying to figure things out. But it’s a new, exciting phase of life worth being thoughtful, intentional, and not terrified about.\n\n# Let’s explore here, together, how to create a mindful return.\n\n## Mindful Return Maternity Leave Course, UK Chapter\n\n \n\nTake the Mindful Return UK Course to ease your transition to working motherhood in the UK.\n\n \n\nRegister\n\n## E-course for Dads\n\nTake the Mindful Return Working Dad Course to ease your transition to working fatherhood.\n\nRegister\n\n## Contact\n\nIf you have questions about Mindful Return, reach out to us here.\n\nE-mail--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIn-Depth Car Seat Safety Resources - Safe in the Seat (https://www.safeintheseat.com/)\nciteturn84search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; \n\n# You just want to get it right. We'll make sure you do.\n\nTurning car seat confusion into calm confidence. Every stage, birth to 13.\n\nCreated by Certified CPSTs\n\nImage: A mother holding a small toddler in her arms\n\n## Trusted by millions of parents. Created by an Internationally Certified CPST (and mom) who gets it.\n\nWhether you’re staring at a wall of car seats for the first time, figuring out when to switch, wondering if that harness is really tight enough, or just wanting that “yep, it’s right” peace of mind, Safe in the Seat is here to help you keep your child safe and your sanity intact.\n\nFinally, Car Seat Safety Simplified\n\n## Certified car seat safety help from one mom to another.\n\n‍You’ve been there, scrolling, searching, and second-guessing.\n‍\nWhich seat is safest? Is it installed right? Can you even take it on a plane?\nWe’ve been there too. That’s why Safe in the Seat exists: to make car seat safety simple, clear, and doable.\nOur team of internationally certified child passenger safety experts (and moms) helps you find the right seat, learn what really matters, and get personalized help when you need it most.Because car seat safety shouldn’t feel complicated, and now, it doesn’t have to.\n\n315\n\n+\n\nThe Comparison Kit wa